      <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(300px,1fr));gap:28px 40px">
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Will testing affect live orders?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">No. We test a staging environment with production-like configuration, and any production confirmation pass uses agreed test accounts and payment sandboxes.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Do you test our payment provider?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">We test your integration with them. Most checkout findings live in how that integration is wired.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">Can you help scope our card data environment?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">Yes. Scope reduction is usually the highest-leverage PCI work, and it is part of the compliance readiness engagement.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--border-default);padding-top:16px">
          <h3 style="font:600 16px/1.3 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:0 0 6px;color:var(--color-ink)">What about third-party scripts on the payment page?</h3>
          <p style="font:400 13.5px/1.55 var(--font-body);color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0;text-wrap:pretty">In scope, and increasingly required by PCI DSS 4.0 Requirement 6.4.3. Skimming through injected scripts remains one of the most common real-world retail breaches.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
